WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.237
Hi, I'm Hani. Sometimes our bodies have extra wiggly energy, and the best way out is through strong, steady pushing. Stay right in your seat for this one, we don't need a wall.

00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:10.592
Sit tall, and press your two palms together hard, right in front of your chest.

00:00:10.592 --> 00:00:17.653
Push your hands into each other as hard as you can. Push, push, push!

00:00:17.653 --> 00:00:24.008
Breathe out slow while you push. Strong and steady, not fast.

00:00:24.008 --> 00:00:30.363
Now stop pushing, and shake your hands out loose. Let them go floppy like noodles.

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:37.424
Now hook your hands under the edge of your chair seat, and pull straight up, hard, like you're trying to lift the chair.

00:00:37.424 --> 00:00:43.073
Breathe out slow the whole time you're pulling.

00:00:43.073 --> 00:00:48.722
Stop, and shake your hands out again.

00:00:48.722 --> 00:00:56.490
Notice how your arms feel now. A little tired is different from wiggly. Tired muscles are calm muscles.

00:00:56.490 --> 00:01:04.257
Rest your hands in your lap whenever you're ready. Your body just did some real work, and your brain gets to feel calmer because of it.

00:01:04.257 --> 00:01:07.788
That's the Heavy Work Reset. Anytime your body feels too wiggly, strong pushing helps it find calm again, no wall required.
